// clinch — the command line of an Axle program, declared once.
//
// This file is the crate's wiring header: it names every module so the build pulls the whole tree
// into the compilation unit, and so the library's public names are the ones a program imports
// from `clinch`. It carries no logic and is GENERATED by `tools/gen_lib.py` — `--check` fails a
// tree where a module is missing from it.
//
// Layers, bottom to top — a module imports from below, never from above or from a sibling
// (doc/ARCHITECTURE.md, tools/check.py):
//
//   core   the vocabulary and the logic, with no operating system: spec, parse, suggest, error, text
//   raw    (not written yet) raw memory, for the seams below: every `unsafe` in the library will be here
//   sys    (not written yet) the seams: one answer per port, every `extern "C"` will be here
//   term   (not written yet) what needs a terminal: prompts, progress, signals
//   app    the front door: `Args` reads the process's command line; `App::run` will tie the rest together
use crate::core::{error, list, parse, spec, suggest, text};
